            <ArticleTitle>Intersphincteric abscess.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 33 patients with an intersphincteric abscess continuous anal pain was the commonest symptom and a lump in the wall of the anal canal the commonest sign.The importance of this condition as a cause of persistent undiagnosed anal pain is stressed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
